al takes precedence over all other strategic considerations.\n- **Winning Moves:** White does not have any immediate 4-in-a-row or winning sequences to counter-attack before defending. Thus, the only valid move is defense.\n\nReason: Black has a "sleeping four" (4-in-a-row blocked at one end) along the diagonal from E5 to H8. The position D4 is the open end of this sequence. To prevent Black from making a 5-in-a-row and winning on the next turn, White must play at D4 to block this line.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "D", "row": 4}'}
